The change touches two files. `InferenceHandler` in `reef/inference/interfaces.py` needs the new `engine_detail(served)` method. `startup_status` in `reef/service/inference_service.py` needs to return it as `engine_detail` while the engine is starting.

One design issue to resolve before editing: `startup_status` takes only `scenario` and `model`. It has no `ServedArtifact`, and the engine handler is looked up from one via `self.engines.handler(served)`. The starting artifact may also have no serving row yet, which the `resolve` docstring implies. The implementer will need to decide how `startup_status` gets the `served` value, or how `engine_detail` takes its input when no row exists. I did not change any code.

